    writes stock.
  - Creating a variant does not create inventory. `createProductVariant` makes no inventory item and no
    productVariantInventoryItem link, so every variant added through the admin is silently untracked and treated
    as infinitely available. Only the seed wires the link up.
  - `manageInventory` and `allowBackorder` are dead columns (product_variant.ts:19-20, plus
    reservation_item.allow_backorder). Nothing reads them: every linked variant is treated as tracked and no
    variant can ever backorder. Honouring them touches buildVariantStock, confirmInventory and complete-cart
    together — see the TODO(inventory) notes in src/workflows/product/utils/build-variant-stock.ts and
    src/api/store/products/[id]/route.ts.
  - `incoming_quantity` is read by the availability projection and never written. There is no restock / purchase
    order concept behind it.
  - No low-stock signal. The seed writes a notification with `triggerType: 'inventory.low_stock'`, but nothing
    emits one.
  - `adjustInventoryLevel` throws when the item has no level at the given location, so fulfilling from a location
    that was never stocked fails rather than falling back.
